#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Monitor Claude and Codex subscription accounts and keep the best one active.

Store: ~/.local/state/ai-accounts (0700). Never prints secrets.

  ai-accounts status [--json]            show accounts, tiers and the active ones
  ai-accounts check [--quiet]            probe every account, switch if a better tier exists
  ai-accounts use <provider> <name>      activate an account by hand (kept while it stays best tier)
  ai-accounts add claude <name>          store a `claude setup-token` token read from stdin
  ai-accounts add codex <name>           create a CODEX_HOME for another ChatGPT login
  ai-accounts label claude <name> <email>
                                         name a Claude account (setup-token tokens cannot read it)
  ai-accounts exec <p[,p]> -- CMD...     run CMD with the active account(s) in its environment
  ai-accounts launch <provider> --model EXACT
                                         prepare nonsecret managed identity for an exact model
  ai-accounts exec <provider> --identity OPAQUE -- CMD...
                                         pin that credential revision; fails closed if unavailable
  ai-accounts exhausted <provider> --identity OPAQUE --model EXACT
                                         report exhausted managed revision; JSON selection result
  ai-accounts run <p> [--model EXACT] [--retry-safe] [--retry-exit N,...] -- CMD...
                                         with --model, select after managed quota failure; replay once
                                         only with --retry-safe (caller guarantees replay is safe)
                                         and only if that provider credential revision changed

Installed as `claude`, `codex` or `loopzero` (symlinks in a directory ahead of the real CLIs
on PATH), it runs the real CLI on the active account(s). Whole loopzero commands are never
replayed. Credentials the caller set itself win.

Claude tiers: 2 = Fable + Opus usable, 1 = Opus only, 0 = none. Codex tiers: 2 = every
model usable, 1 = some models restricted, 0 = none. -1 = unknown (probe failed).
An account is usable below AI_ACCOUNTS_MARGIN (default 0.95) of every limit window.
Claude accounts authenticate with CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN; Codex accounts with CODEX_HOME
("main" is ~/.codex). The monitor keeps the current account while it is in the best
available tier and switches otherwise, preferring the least-used account.

Status reports each window's usage, reset, source and data age. Claude prefers the
OAuth usage API, falling back to the existing one-token model probes.
JSON weekly_used_percent remains the overall 7d window (null if unknown).
Only exec (including --identity) refuses non-owner Claude launches at >=85% of any
reported cached limit (including the Fable sub-cap), or with missing/unreadable
or older than 20 minutes cached status, exiting 3. AI_ACCOUNTS_CLAUDE_OWNER=1 bypasses
this guard; unknown window values stay unknown. This is not fleet-wide enforcement. Direct T3 launches, run
and CLI shims are outside this guard.
"""
